\section{Theory}
In the theory chapter, the term scaling factor denotes the normalization factor.
The symbol table records \(S\) for this meaning and the index points to this section.

\section{Field Study}
In the field-study chapter, the term scale denotes the survey scale.
The symbol table must distinguish this meaning from the theory chapter.

\section{Symbols}
The symbol table records \(S\) for the normalization factor. The survey scale is denoted by the term scale in the field-study chapter and has no dedicated symbol in this document.
The existing index references must continue to resolve.
